[{:adr/related ["90-docs/adr/2607171700-kotobase-storage-protocol-layers.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607172210-kotobase-protocol-layer-extension.edn" "90-docs/protocols/kotoba-resource-protocol.edn"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607172200-kotoba-resource-protocol-0-2-addendum", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-17", :adr/body "# ADR-2607172200: KRP 0.1 landed + 0.2 addendum — WebDAV / OCI / Nostr / SFTP identity mappings\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-17\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki\n**Scope**: `90-docs/protocols/kotoba-resource-protocol.edn`\n\n## Context\n\nADR-2607171700 (kotobase storage/protocol layer, `kotoba-lang/kotobase-protocols`) cites \"KRP 0.1\"\nas its addressing contract, but the KRP document itself (`90-docs/protocols/kotoba-resource-protocol.edn`)\nwas never actually merged to `main` — it existed only on an unmerged branch (the `90-docs` EDN-only\nmigration commit `a7c66a3806e`, diverged from `main` by 454 commits by the time this was noticed).\n`gh api repos/com-junkawasaki/root/contents/90-docs/protocols/kotoba-resource-protocol.edn` returned\n404 against `main` at the time of this ADR. This ADR both lands KRP 0.1 for the first time (content\nunchanged, taken as-authored from that branch) and adds the 0.2 addendum this session's kotobase\nprotocol-extension work needs (WebDAV, OCI Distribution, Nostr, SFTP identity mappings — see\n`90-docs/adr/2607172210-kotobase-protocol-layer-extension.edn` for the repo-layout decision that\ndepends on this).\n\n## Decision\n\n1. Land `90-docs/protocols/kotoba-resource-protocol.edn` (KRP 0.1, four identities: Name/Record/\n   Content/Location, §1-15) unmodified in content from the prior unmerged authoring.\n2. Append a new §16 addendum (non-breaking, no fifth identity axis) mapping WebDAV, OCI Distribution\n   (+ORAS), Nostr, and SFTP onto the existing four identities:\n   - WebDAV path → **Name** (§3.1), with an explicit `:webdav/collection?` flag since WebDAV needs\n     real folder/resource distinction that S3's flat-key convention doesn't have.\n   - OCI tag → Name-like mutable pointer, OCI digest → **Content** (§3.3) — confirms, rather than\n     changes, §10.1's existing \"OCI tag + digest ... WASM, GLB, CAR distribution\" row. ORAS is not a\n     distinct protocol for KRP purposes (same `/v2/...` API, no separate mapping).\n   - Nostr event id / Blossom blob sha256 → **Content** (§3.3), explicitly a domain-specific content\n     hash rather than a general CID — the same carve-out §3.3 already uses for S3 ETags/kotobase\n     fingerprints.\n   - SFTP path → **Location** only (§3.4), no Content/Record mapping, mirroring how git's dumb-HTTP\n     surface is scoped in §8.\n3. Bump the doc's status line to `design baseline 0.1 (2026-07-14); 0.2 addendum 2026-07-17 (§16,\n   non-breaking)` — the addendum is additive, not a restructure; §1-15 are unchanged.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `90-docs/adr/2607171700-kotobase-storage-protocol-layers.edn`'s citation of \"KRP 0.1\" now resolves\n  to a real file on `main` for the first time.\n- The four new protocol handlers scoped in ADR-2607172210 have an explicit, reviewed identity mapping\n  to build against, instead of improvising one per-repo.\n- No existing KRP consumer is affected — §1-15 content is byte-identical to the prior unmerged\n  authoring; only a new §16 was appended and the status line updated.\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2607171700 (kotobase storage/protocol layers — the consumer this KRP gap was discovered from)\n- ADR-2607172210 (protocol-layer-extension decision — WebDAV/OCI/Nostr/SFTP repo layout, depends on\n  this ADR's §16)\n- `90-docs/adr/2607171600-...` (docs EDN-only ADR — the migration this KRP doc was originally authored\n  under, on the unmerged branch this ADR lands from)\n", :db/id -1, :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607172200: KRP 0.1 landed + 0.2 addendum -- WebDAV / OCI / Nostr / SFTP identity mappings", :adr/source-format "edn"}]